WEBVTT

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.950
<b>2012 Kabuki District</b>

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.950
<b>Who Wants To Be A Madaonaire</b>

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.370
Taizo Hasegawa.

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:02.200
He's one question away from becoming a Madaonaire.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.040
Why did he choose to continue?

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.600
A: Because he wears sunglasses.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:09.040
B: Because he has no job.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.800
C: Because this show is rigged.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.180
D: Because he is a Madao.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.310
<b>Madaodog Madaonaire</b>

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:22.650
Hasegawa!

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.150
Hasegawa!

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.780
Hasegawa, it's headed your way!

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:28.940
Catch it!

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:32.150
You better catch it!

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:39.290
How could you drop it?!

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:42.290
Hey! It's you kids again!

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.190
The guards are here!

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.090
Wait up!

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.590
Middle-aged dumb-ass oldies,

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:04.980
also known as Madaos!

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.190
Do you want another chance at life?!

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.320
Do you want to climb up the ladder?!

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.760
Do you have the courage to fight back?!

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.450
This is the show for saving middle-aged dumb-ass oldies!

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.720
Who Wants To Be A Madaonaire?

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:34.380
Hello. I am your host, Nomi.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:39.220
The Madao who makes it to the very end of the game

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:43.000
will receive ten million!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.900
Which Madao will walk away with the money, into a brand new life?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:51.390
Which of the many Madaos in Edo has been given a chance?

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:52.990
Come on down!

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:57.370
Middle-aged darn-amazing oldie!

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.700
Our first contestant lives

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:06.110
on a bench next to the Kabuki District, Hasegawa Taizo-san.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.120
38 years old. Unemployed.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:11.620
Ow!

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.640
It's a pleasure, Hasegawa-san.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:19.170
Why am I here?

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.270
That's what I want to know.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.830
When I woke up, I was lying in the middle

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.600
of a dump like a worn-out rag.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.580
All I could remember was that I had lost everything,

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.700
that I was trash...

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.700
But I held something in my clenched fist!

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.030
<b>Who Wants To Be A Madaonaire?
Golden Ticket
A dream come true for Madaos around the country.</b>

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:40.000
A single ray of light in this filthy dump.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.160
Where did it come from?

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:48.040
I couldn't remember, but I followed the light here.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:52.130
There's one thing I could remember clearly.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.660
My thirst for the ten million.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:01.010
I'm going to take advantage of this last chance I've been given

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.520
and climb out of the garbage heap!

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:08.290
And so, our contestant was a respectable public servant,

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:12.570
but then he lost his job, lost his wife, and now he's a Madao!

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:17.070
Will he be able to claim the ten million and start anew?

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:21.480
His fate rests upon this game show!

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.080
His quest for the ten million begins with the first question for one hundred thousand!

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.860
First question!

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.160
What was the nickname given to the eighth Tokugawa shogun,

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.340
Yoshimune, who introduced the Kyoho reforms?

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:37.480
A: Tyrant Shogun

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:38.830
B: Winter Shogun

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.320
C: Rice Shogun

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.850
D: Money Shogun

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:42.880
Uh...

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.180
This sounds really familiar!

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.350
But I can't remember!

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:48.790
Where have I heard this before?!

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:51.980
Search my memories!

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:57.360
<b>Temple School</b>

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.300
It was...

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.930
It was when...

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:59.860
And these were the Kyoho reforms.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:05.870
<b>New wage system
Rice contributions
Tax policy</b>

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:02.850
After introducing these reforms, Yoshimune became known as...

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:04.510
Oh, that's it!

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.870
I learned about this in class at temple school!

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:08.110
Hm, Hasegawa, answer this question.

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:10.910
What was Yoshimune known as?

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.130
He called on me!

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.800
D-Does the young me know the answer?

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:19.130
<b>History</b>

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:16.850
U-Uh...

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.490
It's over! He's eating his lunch!

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:21.130
He wasn't even listening to the teacher!

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:23.180
Damn, how am I supposed to know the answer?

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:25.140
Uh...

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.560
Huh?

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.150
Who's this cute girl?

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.980
I don't remember her sitting next to me.

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.150
You have rice on your face.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:39.860
Correct.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.550
He was known as the Rice Shogun, just like you.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:46.340
Yeah, he's the Rice Shogun!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.670
And I don't recall experiencing this bittersweet episode?

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.590
I sat next to this cute girl?

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:55.110
Who is she?

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:56.230
I can't remember.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:57.670
Can't remember her name or anything...

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:03.180
Teacher, there's an old man struggling outside!

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:05.680
Stop him!

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.930
<b>C: Rice Shogun.</b>

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.930
I'm over there?!

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.510
Correct!

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:11.780
The answer is C: Rice Shogun!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.940
Hasegawa-san gets his hundred thousand!

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.770
Oh, Hasegawa-san?

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:18.940
Are you unhappy about answering correctly?

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.910
No wonder I couldn't remember her name.

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:24.400
I was watching the scene from a completely different place.

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.830
That brought back some bad memories...

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:31.130
Next, we'll move on to the question for five hundred thousand!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.290
The battle's just begun!

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.800
Pull yourself together!

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:38.210
I don't have time to mope around!

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:39.630
Second question!

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:42.310
In the Battle of Sekigahara,

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.320
which general betrayed the western army

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:45.220
and ensured the eastern army's victory?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.440
A: Tokunaga Hideaki

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.230
B: Kobayakawa Hideaki

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.040
C: Takizawa Hideaki

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:52.760
D: Sorachi Hideaki

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.420
Uh...

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:56.860
I think I've heard this one before, too!

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:57.810
Where?!

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.780
Where did I hear it?!

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.690
Try to remember!

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.470
It was when...

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:07.240
I see. Then we'll take a vote.

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:12.750
<b>Life Lessons</b>

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.380
Yes! This was definitely something I learned at temple school!

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.480
I'm sure of it!

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:13.740
Will you eat the piggy yourselves,

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:16.430
or will you feed it to the lion?

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:19.250
As you were the ones who raised him, you must decide yourselves.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.400
That's a pretty brutal life lesson!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.830
Teacher! We can't do it!

00:08:23.830 --> 00:08:24.590
Of course!

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:27.810
We like steak more than pork chops!

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:29.260
That's why you're crying?!

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:33.860
Yeah! I'm sure lions like beef more than pork!

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.190
What are they supposed to be learning here?

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:41.280
Oh, I remember raising various animals at temple school.

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:44.850
I learned many difficult life lessons that

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.280
I've completely forgotten.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.870
At the moment, the vote is evenly split.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.420
Oh, Hasegawa.

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.850
What's your vote?

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:54.230
Hm? Me?

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:56.850
Which side did I choose?

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.250
Please spare me!

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:00.850
That's my final answer!

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:04.060
How can you betray us at the last second?!

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.740
Are you supposed to be Kobayakawa Hideaki?!

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:10.930
<b>B: Kobayakawa Hideaki</b>

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.930
They were raising a bum, not a pig.

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:10.930
<b>Off seven days a week.</b>

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.430
Correct!

00:09:12.830 --> 00:09:15.190
The five hundred thousand yen is yours!

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:18.310
Hasegawa-san is advancing towards the prize!

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:23.190
Yet he looks to be upset every time he gives a correct answer.

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:27.200
I-I was going to do some hanging around,

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:30.320
when someone stopped me and made me a pet.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:33.580
<b>Chicken   Pig    Rabbit</b>

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:34.000
But I never expected to be used in a lesson for kids.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:38.210
Well, I was doomed to die either way.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:41.000
B-But every time I reflect upon my memories,

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.690
I uncover another hidden trauma.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:47.650
I climb towards the light in the future,

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:50.790
but the darkness in my past drags me down.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.600
Don't try to stop me!

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:56.610
The ten million yen will be mine!

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:03.280
That brings us to the third question, for one million yen!

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.160
These Shock Stickers are all the rage in Edo right now!

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.080
Which of the following characters has their hair parted 7:3?

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.760
A: Little Fatty

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.540
He suddenly switched categories!

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:13.540
B: Cool Body Fat

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.940
C: Fried Chicken Angel

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:17.500
I-I won't be able to search my life for the answer to this question!

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:17.500
D: Super Glasses

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:21.130
Wait, is there an answer inside me?

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:24.990
Even when I've never heard these names before?

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:27.920
Sorry, Piggy.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:29.500
They're so mean.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:32.490
Arguing about whether or not they should eat you after I saved you.

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:33.850
Something's wrong with them.

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:35.020
I-It's her.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.390
The Rice Shogun girl!

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:40.520
She freed me from the school execution?!

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.880
This is the second time you've saved me.

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:49.010
Why are you helping me?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:52.780
You remind me of my dad.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:57.560
My dad used to do a lot of hanging around, the way you do.

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.390
But I would always stop him.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:04.260
He ran off, leaving behind his debts.

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:09.630
Mom and I have no money, but it's okay.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:12.760
As long as we know he's still alive,

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:14.980
we can keep on going.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:21.290
My dream is to become a massive-asset dat-ass object, or Madao,

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:25.150
<b>Who Wants To Be A Madaonaire?</b>

00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:23.460
and participate in this.

00:11:23.460 --> 00:11:25.150
I'll be able to pay off our debts,

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:29.150
and Dad might come back after he sees me on TV.

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:29.150
<b>A: Dat ass</b>

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.810
So I have to study hard at temple school!

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:38.820
But if I run into a question I don't know,

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:41.790
it'll be your turn to save me.

00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:46.670
I'll use a lifeline to call you.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:50.440
So please tell me the answer.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:56.970
Yes, I made a promise to her.

00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:01.770
But before she had a chance to become a massive-asset

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:06.010
dat-ass object, or Madao, the phone rang.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.160
Hey, it's for you, Hasegawa-san.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.960
Someone keeps asking for Piggy.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:19.240
If she knows this number, she must be an acquaintance of yours.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:20.200
Huh?

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:23.260
I can't understand you if you keep crying.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.270
Hello?

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.290
Hey, what's wrong? What happened?

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.130
Piggy...

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:33.880
When I came home from school, Mom was...

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.720
Mom was lying on the floor.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:40.030
I keep shaking her, but she won't wake up!

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.730
What should I do?

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.030
Tell me, Piggy... Piggy...

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:49.810
I failed as her lifeline.

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:55.690
All I could do was stare at the stickers on the phone.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.200
<b>Little Fatty</b>

00:12:56.740 --> 00:12:59.740
Hasegawa-san chooses A: Little Fatty.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:03.260
Is that your final answer?

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.500
That is my final answer.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.290
We'll tell you if he's right after the break!

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:29.610
Correct!

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:31.560
A: Little Fatty!

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.620
Hasegawa-san has answered three questions correctly!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.610
He's made it to one million yen!

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:38.120
Oh! He's fainted!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.300
Hasegawa-san has looked pale after every correct answer,

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:43.120
and now he's collapsed!

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:45.830
H-How could that have happened?

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:48.490
How could I have forgotten?

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:53.090
I'm such a Madao.

00:13:53.610 --> 00:13:55.690
No more...

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:59.730
I don't want to learn how pathetic I am.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:01.600
This is where I belong.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.990
I don't have the right to escape the garbage dump.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.060
Hey, are you okay?

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:09.130
Take him to the infirmary!

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.300
Don't have... Don't have the right...

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:17.860
Please give me the next question.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.630
He stood up!

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:22.960
After fainting and coughing up blood, he continues on!

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:23.620
I'm okay!

00:14:24.020 --> 00:14:27.270
He wants the ten million really bad!

00:14:27.270 --> 00:14:29.300
I want the ten million...

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.570
You bet.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:32.620
I may have lost my will to live,

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:35.630
but my desire for the ten million remains.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.590
This guy's pretty tough.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:39.160
Start making the questions harder.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:40.640
It's time to get rid of him.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:46.670
But I no longer know why I want the money or who it's for...

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:47.700
Question four!

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.810
Name this constellation.

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.110
A: Toilet Minor

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:55.130
I can't quit until I've figured that out...

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:52.720
B: Brave Exkaiser

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:55.110
C: Summer Visor

00:14:58.470 --> 00:15:02.370
It's so warm inside this cardboard box.

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:04.550
It's like a play castle.

00:15:05.090 --> 00:15:06.420
This is fun!

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:13.020
Was she forcing herself to sound happy,

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:16.670
or was she actually enjoying herself?

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:21.440
Piggy, I get to sleep while looking up at the stars.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.940
It's like we're camping.

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:26.430
Do you know what that constellation is?

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.150
She was always smiling.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:40.950
<b>A: Toilet Minor</b>

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:33.990
Correct!

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:37.490
Question five!

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:40.950
Which of the following bento is the most popular at 8-11?

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:44.270
This was all I could manage to do for her...

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:48.200
Oh, this is the one that everyone says is really good!

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:51.390
It still looks safe to eat.

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.910
C-Correct!

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:56.870
Question six!

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:59.100
Which gachapon is very popular with the kids right now?

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:00.150
Keep looking.

00:16:00.150 --> 00:16:01.410
Uh-huh.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.040
Look! This is the one you wanted!

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:08.940
She always had a smile on her face.

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:12.230
<b>A: Kinniguman</b>

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.380
Correct!

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:15.750
I was supposed to be helping her smile,

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:19.180
but it was the other way around.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:22.210
Piggy, I've always dreamed about this.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:22.780
Huh?

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:28.250
Cooking for Dad when he came home early

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:30.480
and chitchatting.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.290
Did you call me Dad?!

00:16:32.490 --> 00:16:34.650
We might live in a cardboard house

00:16:34.650 --> 00:16:36.360
and drink tea from empty cans

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.300
while Dad is always home,

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:41.260
but I'm having a lot of fun right now.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:48.040
This is the first time I've felt at home.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:50.590
So...

00:16:50.590 --> 00:16:52.730
I'll give this to you.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:53.190
<b>Who Wants To Be A Madaonaire?
Golden Ticket
A dream come true for Madaos around the country.</b>

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:54.690
Isn't that...

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:57.940
It's okay now.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:01.190
I got to see Dad...

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:04.840
Hey!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:06.130
Hang in there! Hey!

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:08.030
Hey!

00:17:08.030 --> 00:17:09.620
Come on!

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:12.410
I'm terribly sorry.

00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:15.220
I never dreamed that my wife and daughter

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:17.420
would fall ill while I was away.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:22.590
I should not have insisted on staying away until I found a proper job.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:26.430
I'll find a way to pay their hospital bill...

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:32.140
Money doesn't matter.

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:35.440
Who gives a damn if you have debts?

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:41.700
This is the first time I've felt at home.

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:48.590
It doesn't matter if you live in a dump, as long as you're together.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:54.200
Sorry to interrupt, but we're debt collectors.

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:58.410
Don't give me that crap!

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:01.710
A piece of shit like you is gonna guarantee their debt?!

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:05.840
I promise to pay it off.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.720
So stay away from that family.

00:18:07.970 --> 00:18:11.370
A bum like you won't have enough money!

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:13.180
You know where to get some?

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:14.620
You bet.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.230
I've got this piece of paper I dug out of the trash.

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:19.790
That's bullshit!

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.040
Correct!

00:18:21.860 --> 00:18:24.230
<b>D: Wriggled around</b>

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.630
Our contestant is on a roll!

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:26.020
Answering one question after another!

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:29.220
Hasegawa-san has finally reached seven million five hundred thousand yen!

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:31.240
He's one question away from ten million!

00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:32.610
I-Impossible!

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:34.210
How was he able to answer that question?!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.240
Who is this Madao?!

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:39.470
Hey! Find an impossible question to give him!

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:43.980
He no longer has a pained expression on his face.

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:47.010
What has come over him?!

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.430
Heh, nothing's changed.

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:52.260
But I've finally remembered.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:58.140
I can accept my failures, my pathetic life.

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:02.230
I realize that I'm a hopeless Madao!

00:19:03.020 --> 00:19:06.530
Since I forgot a very important promise.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:08.370
Use this question!

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.800
This tiny article in today's paper!

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:12.530
I'm positive that Madao hasn't read it!

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:20.290
Here is the final question, for ten million yen!

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.040
This is it!

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:26.150
What is the name of the first victim of the new contagious virus,

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:30.550
MADAO 49, who was able to make a full recovery

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:33.300
after treatment on another planet?

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:35.520
A: Nakajima Tomoko

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:37.600
B: Sakurajima Chiharu

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.470
C: Kato Shizue

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.560
D: Terashima Kyoko

00:19:41.560 --> 00:19:43.370
This is a tough one!

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:48.570
Can Hasegawa-san answer the question and win ten million yen?!

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:51.780
Excuse me, can I use a lifeline?

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:52.570
I'd like to call someone.

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.530
Hasegawa-san immediately uses a lifeline!

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:58.580
But do any of his friends know the answer to this question?!

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.600
Nobody's picking up.

00:20:20.730 --> 00:20:22.290
Too bad!

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:27.750
Yeah, hello?

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:31.540
Yeah, it's me.

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:34.810
Sorry about taking so long to call.

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:36.870
This is...

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:42.550
This is Piggy's final answer.

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:49.930
Live a happy life with your mom and dad, Chiharu.

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:51.340
<b>B: Sakurajima Chiharu</b>

00:20:52.470 --> 00:20:58.200
Correct!

00:20:55.550 --> 00:21:00.850
<b>Congratulations!!</b>

00:21:00.850 --> 00:21:02.750
He's done it!

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:06.580
Hasegawa-san has won the ten million!

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:10.180
Our contestant was acquainted with the girl in the final question!

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:11.390
A miracle phone call!

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:12.840
Endless cheers for our Madao!

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:15.640
No, he is no longer a Madao!

00:21:15.640 --> 00:21:19.870
He is a Miracle Madao who's made it to the top!

00:21:22.370 --> 00:21:24.490
Damn, I'm impressed.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:28.060
Then we'll be taking the prize money, big guy.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:30.080
You can call me Madao.

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:35.290
I still have much to learn

00:21:35.290 --> 00:21:36.390
Don't be so modest.

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:41.090
There aren't many people who can pay off ten million so easily.

00:21:41.090 --> 00:21:44.390
I hope you can be as quick on the rest of the debt.

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:46.440
Huh?

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:53.440
<b>Taizo Hasegawa is one question away from becoming a Madaonaire. Why did he choose to continue?</b>

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:53.440
<b>A: Because he wear sunglasses.
C: Because this show is rigged.</b>

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:53.440
<b>B: Because he has no job.
D: Because he is Madao.</b>

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:50.120
The rest of the debt. Twenty million.

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.820
I'm counting on you.

00:21:53.440 --> 00:21:56.910
What?!

00:21:57.450 --> 00:21:57.820
<b>D: Because he is a Madao.</b>

00:21:58.200 --> 00:21:59.950
<b>D: Because he is a Madao.</b>

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:42.050
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:32.840
What was that, you stupid curlyhead?!

00:23:33.050 --> 00:23:34.410
Cut it out already!

00:23:34.410 --> 00:23:35.970
Huh? Why are you so mad?

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Eh?! Do you realize how many weeks it's been since we were last on screen?!

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:41.800
It's been two years for me.

00:23:41.800 --> 00:23:42.370
Oh...

00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:44.930
<b>Presents Are Meant To Be Given Early</b>

00:23:42.370 --> 00:23:42.970
Next time:

00:23:42.970 --> 00:23:44.920
Presents are meant to be given early.

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:49.890
<b>Shinpachi and Kagura haven't said a word since the Chageath Note episode.</b>

00:23:49.890 --> 00:23:54.940
<b>What is the definition of a regular cast member? Nobody even cares anymore.</b>
